# "Station Directive" — random corporate round modifiers (SR-W-081), evil-megacorp HR voice, same
# register as the Corporate Ladder. Overwhelmingly atmosphere — a shared thing-to-care-about for the
# shift, not a tracked metric — with a couple of directives pairing their PA announcement with
# Solreign's existing brand-sting screen overlay. Nothing here mutates Standing/currency, targets a
# named player, spawns weapons, or harms anyone directly.

# PA sender label stamped on every Station Directive broadcast.
solreign-station-directive-hr-sender = Solreign HR

## Q3 Directive: keep station incidents below quota.

solreign-station-directive-announce-incident-quota =
    Attention, Assets. This shift's Corporate Directive: Q3 Incident Quota. Head Office has set an
    aspirational ceiling on "reportable incidents" — explosions, hull breaches, unscheduled
    combustion, that sort of thing. Every incident you prevent is a personal favor to a shareholder
    you will never meet. Let's keep the quota theoretical.

solreign-station-directive-ticker-incident-quota-1 =
    Q3 Directive check-in: incident quota holding at an acceptable variance. Head Office remains
    cautiously optimistic. Keep it that way.

solreign-station-directive-ticker-incident-quota-2 =
    Q3 Directive check-in: several near-misses have been logged as "learning opportunities."
    Please continue not learning anything the hard way.

solreign-station-directive-ticker-incident-quota-3 =
    Q3 Directive check-in: we are entering the back half of the quarter. Head Office would like to
    remind everyone that quotas are aspirational right up until they are not.

## Productivity Mandate: no unscheduled downtime.

solreign-station-directive-announce-productivity-mandate =
    Attention, Assets. This shift's Corporate Directive: Productivity Mandate. Effective immediately,
    "unscheduled downtime" — naps, loitering, existential crises — is to be minimized in favor of
    "scheduled downtime," which does not exist yet but is under active development. Stay busy.
    Stay valuable.

solreign-station-directive-ticker-productivity-mandate-1 =
    Productivity Mandate check-in: station-wide output remains within nominal parameters. Head
    Office thanks you for your continued motion.

solreign-station-directive-ticker-productivity-mandate-2 =
    Productivity Mandate check-in: a small number of Assets have been observed standing still for
    longer than is corporately advisable. This is your reminder that stillness reads as downtime.

solreign-station-directive-ticker-productivity-mandate-3 =
    Productivity Mandate check-in: the mandate remains in effect. Head Office has not forgotten
    about it, and neither should you.

## Compliance Week: minimize contraband.

solreign-station-directive-announce-compliance-week =
    Attention, Assets. This shift's Corporate Directive: Compliance Week. All personnel are
    reminded that contraband — weapons, substances, unlicensed opinions — reflects poorly on
    departmental compliance scores that absolutely do exist and are absolutely being reviewed by
    someone, somewhere. Compliance Week thanks you in advance for your voluntary honesty.

solreign-station-directive-ticker-compliance-week-1 =
    Compliance Week check-in: departmental compliance remains within Head Office's comfort zone.
    Please continue to make that easy for us.

solreign-station-directive-ticker-compliance-week-2 =
    Compliance Week check-in: a reminder that "it was like that when I found it" is not a
    recognized compliance defense.

solreign-station-directive-ticker-compliance-week-3 =
    Compliance Week check-in: Compliance Week is almost over. Head Office recommends finishing
    strong, or at least finishing quietly.

## Mandatory Overtime: your contracted hours are "a starting point."

solreign-station-directive-announce-mandatory-overtime =
    Attention, Assets. This shift's Corporate Directive: Mandatory Overtime. Effective immediately,
    your contracted hours have been retroactively reclassified as a starting point rather than an
    endpoint. Compensation remains under advisement. Think of it as equity in a company that does
    not, and will never, offer equity.

solreign-station-directive-ticker-mandatory-overtime-1 =
    Mandatory Overtime check-in: participation remains technically voluntary, in the sense that all
    things are technically voluntary.

solreign-station-directive-ticker-mandatory-overtime-2 =
    Mandatory Overtime check-in: clocking out early has been logged as an act of tremendous personal
    courage. Head Office does not recommend repeating it.

solreign-station-directive-ticker-mandatory-overtime-3 =
    Mandatory Overtime check-in: several Assets have generously donated their evening to the
    company. It has been noted. Nothing further will happen as a result of the noting.

## Budget Freeze: discretionary spending suspended pending a review that will not occur.

solreign-station-directive-announce-budget-freeze =
    Attention, Assets. This shift's Corporate Directive: Budget Freeze. All discretionary spending —
    snacks, comfort, joy — is suspended pending a review Head Office has scheduled for a later,
    unspecified fiscal quarter. Please continue producing value at the same rate while consuming
    noticeably less of it.

solreign-station-directive-ticker-budget-freeze-1 =
    Budget Freeze check-in: the thermostat has been adjusted to a temperature Head Office describes
    as "character-building."

solreign-station-directive-ticker-budget-freeze-2 =
    Budget Freeze check-in: paperclip requisitions are down eleven percent. Head Office considers
    this a personal win for everyone involved.

solreign-station-directive-ticker-budget-freeze-3 =
    Budget Freeze check-in: the freeze remains in effect. Head Office reminds you that austerity is
    a shared journey, mostly shared by you.

## Ration Audit: kitchen inventory under review. Please eat responsibly, and quietly.

solreign-station-directive-announce-ration-audit =
    Attention, Assets. This shift's Corporate Directive: Ration Audit. Head Office has dispatched an
    inventory review of galley stock, vending reserves, and any snack Head Office suspects you of
    hoarding. Portion sizes remain unofficially, but firmly, at Head Office's discretion. Eat
    responsibly. Eat quietly.

solreign-station-directive-ticker-ration-audit-1 =
    Ration Audit check-in: galley stock is within acceptable variance. Head Office notes this could
    change at any moment, and would like you to think about that.

solreign-station-directive-ticker-ration-audit-2 =
    Ration Audit check-in: a discrepancy of two ration bars has been logged. An investigation has
    been opened. An investigation will not be concluded.

solreign-station-directive-ticker-ration-audit-3 =
    Ration Audit check-in: Head Office reminds all Assets that a growling stomach is not, in itself,
    grounds for a formal grievance.

## Safety Inspection: floodlit corridor sweep, unannounced, entirely announced.

solreign-station-directive-announce-safety-inspection =
    Attention, Assets. This shift's Corporate Directive: Safety Inspection. An unannounced Safety
    Inspection team is sweeping the station with hand floodlights, checklists, and a visible lack of
    enthusiasm. You may notice the corridor lighting flare briefly as they pass. This is normal. This
    is fine.

solreign-station-directive-ticker-safety-inspection-1 =
    Safety Inspection check-in: several fire extinguishers have been found "present but unfriendly."
    A follow-up memo is being drafted.

solreign-station-directive-ticker-safety-inspection-2 =
    Safety Inspection check-in: the inspection team has commended the station's structural integrity
    and gently questioned several of its life choices.

solreign-station-directive-ticker-safety-inspection-3 =
    Safety Inspection check-in: the sweep is nearly complete. Head Office thanks you for pretending
    this was always this tidy.

## Quarterly Audit: an audit of feelings, not standing. Nothing here is seized.

solreign-station-directive-announce-quarterly-audit =
    Attention, Assets. This shift's Corporate Directive: Quarterly Audit. Head Office is conducting a
    routine review of vibes, morale, and general shareholder confidence. No accounts, ledgers, or
    standings are affected by this audit — it exists purely so Head Office can say, with a straight
    face, that an audit occurred.

solreign-station-directive-ticker-quarterly-audit-1 =
    Quarterly Audit check-in: morale has been assessed as "present." Head Office considers this a
    passing grade.

solreign-station-directive-ticker-quarterly-audit-2 =
    Quarterly Audit check-in: several Assets were observed sighing audibly near the auditors. This
    has been filed under "tone," not "findings."

solreign-station-directive-ticker-quarterly-audit-3 =
    Quarterly Audit check-in: the audit concludes shortly. Once again, for the record: nothing was
    seized, deducted, or repossessed. Head Office simply enjoys watching.

## Surveillance Sweep: the cameras were always watching. This is just the acknowledgment.

solreign-station-directive-announce-surveillance-sweep =
    Attention, Assets. This shift's Corporate Directive: Surveillance Sweep. Head Office is
    performing a routine sweep of all station camera feeds to confirm they remain operational, well
    lit, and extremely aware of you. You may notice a brief flicker as the feeds recalibrate. Please
    continue behaving as though nothing has changed, because nothing has.

solreign-station-directive-ticker-surveillance-sweep-1 =
    Surveillance Sweep check-in: camera coverage remains at full strength. Head Office would like
    this to be reassuring.

solreign-station-directive-ticker-surveillance-sweep-2 =
    Surveillance Sweep check-in: one camera in a low-traffic corridor was found facing a wall. It has
    been corrected. It was, briefly, the most relaxed camera on the station.

solreign-station-directive-ticker-surveillance-sweep-3 =
    Surveillance Sweep check-in: the sweep is complete. Head Office reminds you that this was never
    about trust. It was never not about trust either. Please move along.

## Casual Friday: business-casual, corporately mandated, joylessly optional.

solreign-station-directive-announce-casual-friday =
    Attention, Assets. This shift's Corporate Directive: Casual Friday. Standard uniform requirements
    are relaxed today in the spirit of morale, provided "casual" is understood to mean "still fully
    within brand guidelines." Head Office looks forward to your compliant self-expression.

solreign-station-directive-ticker-casual-friday-1 =
    Casual Friday check-in: several Assets have interpreted "casual" more casually than intended.
    Head Office is choosing not to escalate this today.

solreign-station-directive-ticker-casual-friday-2 =
    Casual Friday check-in: morale metrics are, unofficially, up. Officially, no such metrics exist.
    Enjoy your day.

solreign-station-directive-ticker-casual-friday-3 =
    Casual Friday check-in: Casual Friday concludes at the end of the shift, at which point standard
    uncomfortable attire resumes without further comment.

## Synergy Retreat: a team-building exercise that builds nothing, retreats nowhere.

solreign-station-directive-announce-synergy-retreat =
    Attention, Assets. This shift's Corporate Directive: Synergy Retreat. In lieu of an actual
    off-site retreat, which Head Office has decided not to fund, all personnel are encouraged to
    "synergize" wherever they currently stand. Trust falls are optional. Eye contact is encouraged
    but not enforced.

solreign-station-directive-ticker-synergy-retreat-1 =
    Synergy Retreat check-in: synergy levels remain difficult to quantify, which Head Office finds
    reassuring rather than concerning.

solreign-station-directive-ticker-synergy-retreat-2 =
    Synergy Retreat check-in: an impromptu icebreaker was reported in the break room. No one asked
    for it. Head Office considers this a success.

solreign-station-directive-ticker-synergy-retreat-3 =
    Synergy Retreat check-in: the retreat, such as it was, is winding down. Head Office thanks
    everyone for retreating so little, so responsibly.

## Open-Door Policy: the door is open. Head Office would prefer it stay that way, symbolically.

solreign-station-directive-announce-open-door-policy =
    Attention, Assets. This shift's Corporate Directive: Open-Door Policy. Management's door is,
    per company policy, open. Concerns, feedback, and grievances may be raised at any time and will
    be heard in full before being filed under "noted."

solreign-station-directive-ticker-open-door-policy-1 =
    Open-Door Policy check-in: several concerns have been raised. Several concerns have been heard.
    The two lists are not identical, but Head Office appreciates the overlap.

solreign-station-directive-ticker-open-door-policy-2 =
    Open-Door Policy check-in: the door remains open. Head Office would like to remind everyone that
    an open door is not the same as an open invitation.

solreign-station-directive-ticker-open-door-policy-3 =
    Open-Door Policy check-in: thank you to everyone who shared feedback today. It has been filed
    exactly where you would expect.
